{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491013-speculation-on-never-was-5th-edition-content","id":1491013,"title":"Speculation on never-was 5th edition content?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-22T11:22:15-07:00","id":1491013,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Speculation on never-was 5th edition content?","content":"If V5 had novels before the corebook came out, and you got to write them, what are they about? Something from BJD I'm guessing? The Tremere getting their comeuppance; they're gone now, hello Salubri?<br /> <br /> You get your own 13 clan novel saga to develop...<br /> <br /> What is the story about and what happens in it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T14:53:23-07:00","id":1491047,"title":"","content":"Lucita de Aragon succumbs to the Beckoning, and after traversing thousands of miles of desert to meet with the Elders, realizes the Gehenna War was nothing more than the Elders saying &quot;Fine, you think it's so easy to make everything fair and equal? It's all yours, Neonates. Fuck it up as best you can&quot; and sitting back playing Euchre. Just like the Antediluvians did to the Methuselahs, and exactly like the Methuselahs did to the Elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T22:45:13-07:00","id":1491159,"title":"","content":"It would be really nice to really see the Gehenna going on, like, the perceptive characters (like Beckett) noticing &quot;wow, why the hell are elders leaving and vanishing like that? what is going on&quot;<br /> It is a nice mystery to uncover, and you I would have some chars being elders, or getting into places they shouldn't. To get that Lovecraft's Nameless City vibe. And the notion that... there are terrible thing throughout the night... <br /> <br /> Some elders would learn terrible ways to resist the Beckoning. Caitiffs and Thinbloods would start to show some real bite and numbers. The Burning Times would be back.and some vamps wouldn't be able do adapt in time. There would be a bit of horror without you knowing who is going to make it.<br /> We would see where the former Icon Chars are at, even if a little. <br /> <br /> I would try not to make everyone just kind of coincidently stumble upon all the events like Beckett does, it would be distributed between the characters, like the Dark Ages Novel. So first I would begin with the simple mystery of &quot;where the hell did my grandsire went, and why is my own sire acting weird?&quot; and then &quot;why is he gone?&quot;. Dealing with a Camarilla facing a terrible crisis, where its members are vanishing, cities are losing their strongest members. Anarchs are getting hungry for territory, and while the Sabbat leave some for these buzzards, it isn't going away, it is retreating into the shadows... Fear and Pandemonium, while the Prince tries to get all in order. <br /> <br /> <br /> Certainly there would be more of Ashirra showing. Maybe a bit of the Vermillion Wedding even. It would be, all in all, a big showcase of the setting through tense, afraid and curious eyes.<br /> In the end, it would be made somewhat evident that as much as the elders were afraid of the Gehenna and even might've incited the young to fear it and bicker between themselves so as to keep them safe, in the end.... the Gehenna came for the Elders, and not the Young.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}